## Proposed per-tailnet seam for confirmation

Live review confirms this is a config-resolution/composition-root problem; the #453 engine and checkpoint contracts do not need redesign.

Recommendation:

```yaml
tailnets:
  - name: alpha.example.com
    objectstore:
      flow: { endpoint: ..., region: ..., bucket: ..., prefix: ... }
      audit: { endpoint: ..., region: ..., bucket: ..., prefix: ... }
```

- retain `collectors.flowlogs.objectstore` and the future `collectors.auditlogs.objectstore` only for legacy/single-tailnet mode;
- in multi-tailnet mode, never inherit a global destination or credential into an entry;
- require every runtime selecting an object-store signal to have its own complete block;
- reject exact duplicate endpoint/region/bucket/prefix/path-style feeds across tailnets rather than recreate cross-attribution through explicit duplicates;
- keep ingestion source selection global per signal for this issue; mixed poll/object-store modes per runtime are out of scope;
- retain literal configured name, including `-`, separately from display/telemetry name and use it for `CheckpointScope.Tailnet`;
- reveal each entry credentials only while constructing that runtime provider;
- fail fast on immutable structural client-construction errors; request-time auth/network errors remain scheduler-visible runtime health.

Please confirm this public YAML shape, no-inheritance rule, duplicate-feed rejection and fail-fast policy. Config RED tests can proceed without changing the frozen collector engine.

## Pre-implementation durability decision record

The premise remains valid at `d701ebe45ffabe34b5ccf1d3923372ff38270759`: HEC/webhook processor return is an in-memory handoff, while metrics use a periodic reader and logs use a batch processor. Deleting a WAL entry immediately after `Process`/emit would still permit acknowledged loss.

Recommended contract pending owner confirmation:

- one process-global, optional local file WAL, disabled by default;
- authenticate, route, decode and semantically validate the complete batch before append;
- HTTP success immediately after owner-only entry + file fsync + rename + directory fsync;
- apply asynchronously to the exact stored tailnet route;
- complete only after processor application, the matching tailnet flow-rollup drain, and metric/log `ForceFlush`;
- never claim backend durability or exactly once: a crash or ambiguous export failure after export and before completion can replay and duplicate;
- no TTL or automatic eviction of uncommitted entries; full capacity fails new admission with 503;
- corruption fails closed and preserves the entry for operator action;
- recommended default `max_bytes: 268435456`; Helm must state that `emptyDir` is not durable across pod rescheduling.

The storage package, filesystem integrity tests and receiver-independent envelope work can proceed separately. Receiver ACK/completion wiring and public defaults wait for this policy confirmation.
